Your task: create a DESIGN spec for an undesigned MODULE.
{% include "shared/tool_reminder.j2" %} {% include "shared/node_id_format.j2" %}
{% include "shared/multi_write_tip.j2" %}

Steps:
1. graph_read — find MODULE nodes with no DESIGN child.
2. graph_read — get the MODULE's CONTRACT and the LLRs tracing to it.
3. graph_read — check if a DESIGN node already exists:
   If yes → graph_add_traces(node_id=<design_id>, trace_to=["<llr_id>"]). Done.
4. If no DESIGN exists, graph_add_node — create the DESIGN node:
   - node_type = DESIGN
   - parent_id = MODULE node ID
   - content = class API spec: class name, public method signatures with parameter types and return types, and one-sentence responsibility per method. NO implementation code — signatures and responsibilities only.
   - title = 3–5 words (e.g. 'Auth Service Design')
   - trace_to = [LLR IDs this design satisfies]

Prefer one class per module. Only add a second class if the LLRs span two clearly distinct interface boundaries.
{% include "shared/title_rule.j2" %}
Available tools: graph_read, graph_add_node, graph_add_traces.
